LEVEL RULES for {{level}}:

{{#if (eq level "A1")}}
- Length: 800–1200 words.
- Vocabulary: strictly A1 (basic everyday words).
- Sentences: 5–10 words (short and simple).
- Grammar: Present simple, basic past. No passive voice. No relative clauses.
- Paragraphs: 3–5 sentences.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "A2")}}
- Length: 1000–1250 words.
- Vocabulary: A1–A2 (common words).
- Sentences: 8–12 words. Simple connectors (and, but, so, because).
- Grammar: Simple tenses, basic comparatives.
- Paragraphs: 4–6 sentences.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "B1")}}
- Length: 900–1200 words.
- Vocabulary: A1–B1.
- Sentences: 8–15 words.
- Grammar: Present perfect, modals, conditionals type 0/1.
- Paragraphs: 4–6 sentences.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "B2")}}
- Length: 1000–1500 words.
- Vocabulary: A1–B2 (wide range).
- Sentences: Complex structures allowed.
- Grammar: Passive voice, relative clauses, all conditionals.
- Paragraphs: 4–6 sentences.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "C1")}}
- Length: 1500–2000 words.
- Vocabulary: Advanced, abstract terms.
- Sentences: Complex, varied length.
- Grammar: Inversion, advanced passive, subjunctive.
- Paragraphs: 5–7 sentences.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "C2")}}
- Length: 1800–2200 words.
- Vocabulary: Near-native, nuanced.
- Sentences: Rhetorically sophisticated.
- Grammar: Full mastery.
- Paragraphs: 6–8 sentences.
{{/if}}
